Listing 11.7 HUD::UpdateCrosshair Implementation
void HUD::UpdateCrosshair(float deltaTime)
{
// Reset to regular cursor
mTargetEnemy = false;
// Make a line segment
const float cAimDist = 5000.0f;
Vector3 start, dir;
mGame->GetRenderer()->GetScreenDirection(start, dir);
LineSegment l(start, start + dir * cAimDist);
// Segment cast
PhysWorld::CollisionInfo info;
if (mGame->GetPhysWorld()->SegmentCast(l, info))
{
// Check if this actor has a target component
for (auto tc : mTargetComps)
{
if (tc->GetOwner() == info.mActor)
{
mTargetEnemy = true;
break;
}
}
}
}
Drawing the crosshair texture is straightforward. In HUD::Draw, you simply check the value of
mTargetEnemy and draw the corresponding texture in the center of the screen. You pass in
2.0f as the scale of the texture, as well:
